  "name": "Hong Kong at Night",
  "summary": "\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/10601/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/10601/10601.avif\"\n         title=\"Victoria Harbour\"\n         alt=\"Black and white photo showing a night scene showing the skyline of Hong Kong with victoria harbour in the centre\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"10601\" loading=\"eager\"  fetchpriority=\"high\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eVictoria Harbour\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e",
  "content": "\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/10601/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/10601/10601.avif\"\n         title=\"Victoria Harbour\"\n         alt=\"Black and white photo showing a night scene showing the skyline of Hong Kong with victoria harbour in the centre\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"10601\" loading=\"eager\"  fetchpriority=\"high\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eVictoria Harbour\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photo/9812/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photo/9812/9812.avif\"\n         title=\"Central\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9812\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eCentral\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/10603/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/10603/10603.avif\"\n         title=\"Queen\u0026rsquo;s Road Central\"\n         alt=\"Black and white photo of a street from above at night, lined by tall buildings. A truck with two people at the rear sits at the junction while some streaked lights suggests a car passes\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"999\"\n\t\t id=\"10603\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eQueen\u0026rsquo;s Road Central\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"diptych\"\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/9212/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/9212/9212.avif\"\n         title=\"Tamar Street\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9212\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eTamar Street\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/9211/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/9211/9211.avif\"\n         title=\"Admiralty\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9211\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eAdmiralty\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/9303/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/9303/9303.avif\"\n         title=\"Arsenal Street\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9303\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eArsenal Street\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/9209/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/9209/9209.avif\"\n         title=\"Escalators II\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9209\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eEscalators II\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/9304/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/9304/9304.avif\"\n         title=\"Queen\u0026rsquo;s Road East Underpass\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9304\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eQueen\u0026rsquo;s Road East Underpass\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\u003cdiv class=\"diptych\"\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photo/9610/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photo/9610/9610.avif\"\n         title=\"Pei Ho Street Market I\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9610\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003ePei Ho Street Market I\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photo/9611/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photo/9611/9611.avif\"\n         title=\"Pei Ho Street Market II\"\n         alt=\"TODO alt text\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"9611\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003ePei Ho Street Market II\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\u003c/div\u003e\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/10602/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/10602/10602.avif\"\n         title=\"Old Bailey Street\"\n         alt=\"Black \u0026amp; white photo of a street corner with pedestrian crossing indicator in front of a large concrete pillar which is flanked by metal fences and an older brick building\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"10602\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eOld Bailey Street\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\n\n\n\u003cfigure\u003e\n\t\u003ca href=\"/photos/10606/\"\u003e\n\t\u003cimg src=\"/photos/10606/10606.avif\"\n         title=\"Central Plaza\"\n         alt=\"Black \u0026amp; white photo looking sligtly upwards at the facards of three skyscrapers\"\n\t\t height=\"1000\"\n\t\t width=\"1000\"\n\t\t id=\"10606\" loading=\"lazy\"  fetchpriority=\"auto\" /\u003e \n    \u003c/a\u003e\u003cfigcaption\u003e\n            \u003cp\u003eCentral Plaza\u003c/p\u003e\n        \u003c/figcaption\u003e\n\t\u003c/figure\u003e\n\n\u003cp\u003eI took these photos in June and August of 2018. A number of them were taken\nafter I went to an opening night event for an exhibition of photos by one of my\nfaviourite photographers \u003ca href=\"https://www.michaelkenna.com/\"\u003eMichael Kenna\u003c/a\u003e, who was\nalso at the opening for a Q\u0026amp;A. I arrived at \u003ca href=\"https://bluelotus-gallery.com/\"\u003eBlue Lotus\nGallery\u003c/a\u003e\u0026rsquo;s location in Chai Wan, on the very\nEastern end of Hong Kong, on time for when the event was starting only to find\nout that the event and exhibition wasn\u0026rsquo;t there \u0026mdash; but rather it was a pop up in\nCentral, at the other end of the island. Thankfully there was someone from the\ngallery still there to tell me where I should be, and she let me ride in her\ntaxi to the exhibition.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI arrived after the Q\u0026amp;A had finished so I went up to Kenna for a quick chat \u0026mdash;\nI don\u0026rsquo;t remember exactly what was said, but I do remember that he patiently\nlistened to me nervously ramble mostly about my own photography, and I found out\nthat he\u0026rsquo;d also found that it was partiucularly hard to get your film hand\nchecked at airports in South Korea. After having a good look at the exhibition,\nI headed out into the city feeling quite inspired and took some of the above\nphotos.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003c/br\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eI bought a mini tripod while I was in Hong Kong, but only after I\u0026rsquo;d taken most\nof these photos so for those I had to improvise ways to stabalise the camera\nwell enough for a long exposure. I had to find walls or sometimes bins on which\nI could rest my camera, using my rucksack to angle the camera correctly. The\nmini tripod I bought didn\u0026rsquo;t come with a tripod head, so even once I had that it\nwas still awkward.\u003c/p\u003e\n\u003cp\u003eEvery photo in the series was shot on my Hasselblad 500C/M with either a 60mm\nf/3.5 CF or 150mm f/4 CF lens using Ilford HP5+ shot at ISO 800 and developed\nin Ilfotec HC 1:49 for 11 minutes. I scanned them with an Epson V800 and edited\nthem in darktable.\u003c/p\u003e",
  "url": "https://samsm.ch/hong-kong-at-night/",
